WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.510
In this lesson, you will learn to tell a story in scenes: use broadcast messages so characters take turns, and change backdrops between scenes.

2
00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:14.670
A story has a beginning, a middle and an end.

3
00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:19.640
In Scratch, each scene can have its own backdrop and characters.

4
00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:23.960
When the Cat finishes talking, it broadcasts a message.

5
00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:27.690
The Dog waits for that message, then replies.

6
00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:30.030
No guessing how long to wait!

7
00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:33.240
Broadcast a message like “scene 2”.

8
00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:39.460
The sprites and the stage react: switch the backdrop, show or hide characters.

9
00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:43.680
“say for 2 seconds” waits before the next block runs.

10
00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:49.120
Use waits to give readers time — about 1 second for every 3 words.

11
00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:52.570
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

12
00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:57.480
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
